@startuml
!include ../11-bmc/_style.iuml
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EBF5FB
  BorderColor #2E86C1
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FEF9E7
}
title Should you take an angel investor?
start
if (Do you need the money to reach the first customer?\n(about SAR 55,000, minimum SAR 33,000)) then (no, self-fund)
  if (Does someone bring buyers, not just cash?\n(ex-procurement director, contractor-group owner)) then (yes)
    :Strategic advisor: 0.5 to 2 % equity,
    earned over 2 years, little or no cash; <<#82E0AA>>
  else (no)
    :No angel now; <<#D5DBDB>>
  endif
  if (3 to 5 paying customers, and you want to hire\nor go full-time before revenue covers it?) then (yes)
    :Raise an angel round, SAR 300k to 500k,
    convertible note with a Saudi lawyer; <<#AED6F1>>
  else (no)
    :Stay self-funded, lean plan; <<#D5DBDB>>
  endif
  if (Year-3 decision: become a licensed lender? (docs/12)) then (yes)
    :Institutional round (VC and fintech investors),
    SAR 5M+ capital, not angels; <<#F8C471>>
  else (no)
  endif
else (yes)
  :Cut to the SAR 33,000 minimum first,
  then look for a co-founder who invests; <<#F8C471>>
endif
stop
legend right
  <b>What angel money costs (example, not market data)</b>
  Raise SAR 300,000 at a SAR 3M pre-money value
  so you give away <b>9.1 %</b>.
  At a SAR 15M exit that stake is worth <b>SAR 1.36M</b>
  That is <b>4.5x</b> what the angel paid.
  ....
  Worth more than an angel now:
  a <b>Saudi sales co-founder</b> (20 to 40 %, earned over 4 years).
endlegend
@enduml
